  "section_notes": "The final text removes any automatic sales ban for models above 5% failure, replacing it with regulator review, corrective action and retesting, which protects Northwind's Hearth 10. Per-model numeric failure rates go to customers but not to the public, and recall is left to regulator discretion with no numeric mandatory trigger at 8 per 100,000, which protects Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9. The six-year retrofit deadline and the 36-month suppression deadline sit inside the acceptable ranges."
